{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/category_directory_card

    One poster of an area, drawn by the areas partial inside a list item of its
    grid, on the root's directory and on a category page organised by area
    alike. The list item belongs to the areas partial so that this partial is a
    whole element on its own, which is what the template lint renders. The
    poster is the card as a whole: its media fills it, the area's crests and the
    kind tag sit on top, and its name, description and trigger sit on a solid
    base in the area's own colour, so the text keeps the pair the editor
    certified whatever the photograph is.

    The open poster says so in words as well as with its ring: an "Open" tag
    under the kind tag, always in the markup and shown by the poster's open
    class alone, which the panel module moves, so the state never reads by
    colour alone. Assistive technology hears it from the control's
    aria-expanded instead, so the tag is hidden from it.

    At rest a poster carries no number. Under a search or a filter a pill below
    the kind tag says how many results the area holds (in the zero colours when
    it holds none) and describes the control. The pill is always in the
    document, hidden at rest, and the article carries the count, the formatted
    result count and the pill's words, because the client rewrites all of them
    after a filter change - silently, with no live region - and puts the words
    back on the pill when a request fails.

    The control is inside the heading and the stylesheet stretches it over the
    whole poster, so an area is one Tab stop. Without JavaScript it is a link: to
    this page with the area's panel open, to this page without it on the open
    poster, and to the area's own page on a poster with nothing to open, whose
    accessible name says so. The panel module turns the first two into buttons.
    The film's controls come after the control in the document, so the area is
    the first stop and its three controls the next, each naming the area.

    The colours travel in one style attribute on the poster: the band, the ink
    and, on a poster with no still, the watermark's opacity and the crest it is
    cut from. That is a CSS context, which Mustache escaping does not protect, so
    the server builds it from a closed vocabulary alone - two hex colours, a
    two-decimal number and a url styleurl::safe() passed (see population::mark()).
    The watermark is written twice and the stylesheet shows one: under the text
    for the card, in the thumbnail for the list view. It is decorative and hidden
    from assistive technology; the crest list is what a screen reader is given.

    The card element is the cover film's band (its data-region), which the film
    module binds its hover, its observer and its playing class to; the still is
    written first and the film second, and the stylesheet states the stack. The
    film carries no controls attribute and preloads nothing, so a reader without
    JavaScript sees the still and nothing half-working. The cluster and the bar
    carry the film module's own mark and not the listing module's, because the
    film module also runs where the listing module does not.

    Every hook the client modules read is a data attribute: the poster's region,
    its id, whether it opens, its name, and the shell a panel needs before its
    rows arrive - the title's address and the call to action's address and label
    - plus the control's and the trigger's regions. The trigger carries its three
    words (open, close, and an empty poster's "no courses yet") so the client
    swaps them without composing anything.

    A poster can change whether it opens without a reload: an area with no
    course is a link at rest and opens a panel under a criterion, and the client
    applies filters in place. So both states are always written - the trigger's
    words, the chevron (hidden by the stylesheet on an empty poster) and the
    visually hidden note saying the link opens the area's page, hidden while the
    poster opens a panel - and the client flips the class, the attribute, the
    note and the control.

    A listed but not public area, on the anonymous shell, is a text poster: its
    colours and its name, with no still, no film, no crest and no watermark,
    because the public file route refuses the files of a category that is not
    public.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "id": 7,
        "name": "Volunteer Brigade & Rescue",
        "url": "https://example.com/course/index.php?categoryid=7",
        "description": "Continuing education, technical courses and organisation events.",
        "hasdescription": true,
        "style": "--dim-card-band: #0a4a85; --dim-card-ink: #ffffff;",
        "imageurl": "https://example.com/pluginfile.php/31/theme_dimensions/categorycover/7/abc/capa.jpg",
        "hasimage": true,
        "eager": true,
        "hasvideo": true,
        "videourl": "https://example.com/pluginfile.php/31/theme_dimensions/categorycovervideo/7/def/capa.mp4",
        "videotype": "video/mp4",
        "badges": [
            {"url": "https://example.com/pluginfile.php/31/theme_dimensions/categorybadge1/7/abc/crest-alpha.png", "alt": "crest alpha"}
        ],
        "hasbadges": true,
        "badgeslabel": "Institutions",
        "hasmark": false,
        "markfolder": false,
        "count": 26,
        "linkable": true,
        "istext": false,
        "variant": "photo",
        "expandable": true,
        "isopen": false,
        "controlurl": "https://example.com/course/index.php?categoryid=3&q=rescue&open=7#dim-panel",
        "hascontrolurl": true,
        "shell": {"titleurl": "https://example.com/course/index.php?categoryid=7", "ctaurl": "https://example.com/course/index.php?categoryid=7&q=rescue&sort=recent", "ctalabel": "Go to Volunteer Brigade & Rescue · 18 more results", "resultlabel": "26 results", "resultcount": "26"},
        "results": {"has": true, "label": "26 results", "count": "26", "iszero": false}
    }
}}
<article class="dim-poster dim-poster--{{variant}}{{#hasvideo}} dim-poster--film{{/hasvideo}}{{^expandable}} dim-poster--empty{{/expandable}}{{#isopen}} dim-poster--open{{/isopen}}" id="dim-area-{{id}}" data-region="dim-area" data-categoryid="{{id}}" data-name="{{name}}" data-titleurl="{{shell.titleurl}}" data-ctaurl="{{shell.ctaurl}}" data-ctalabel="{{shell.ctalabel}}" data-expandable="{{#expandable}}1{{/expandable}}{{^expandable}}0{{/expandable}}" data-count="{{count}}" data-resultcount="{{results.count}}" data-resultlabel="{{results.label}}" style="{{style}}">
    <div class="dim-poster__card" data-region="dim-cover-media">
        <div class="dim-poster__media">
            {{#hasimage}}
            <img class="dim-poster__img" src="{{imageurl}}" alt=""{{^eager}} loading="lazy"{{/eager}} decoding="async" width="560" height="315">
            {{/hasimage}}
            {{#hasvideo}}
            <video class="dim-poster__video" data-region="dim-cover-video" muted playsinline loop preload="none">
                <source src="{{videourl}}" type="{{videotype}}">
            </video>
            {{/hasvideo}}
            {{#hasmark}}
            <span class="dim-poster__mark{{#markfolder}} dim-poster__mark--folder{{/markfolder}}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {{/hasmark}}
        </div>
        <div class="dim-poster__top">
            {{#hasbadges}}
            <ul class="dim-poster__crests" role="list" aria-label="{{badgeslabel}}" data-region="dim-card-crests">
                {{#badges}}
                <li class="dim-poster__crest"><img src="{{url}}" alt="{{alt}}" width="48" height="53" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></li>
                {{/badges}}
            </ul>
            {{/hasbadges}}
            {{^hasbadges}}
            <span class="dim-poster__nocrests"></span>
            {{/hasbadges}}
            <span class="dim-poster__tags"><span class="dim-poster__kind">{{#str}}category_kind_category, theme_dimensions{{/str}}</span><span class="dim-poster__open" aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-eye" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{#str}}category_poster_open, theme_dimensions{{/str}}</span><span class="dim-poster__pill{{#results.iszero}} dim-poster__pill--zero{{/results.iszero}}" id="dim-area-results-{{id}}" data-region="dim-poster-pill"{{^results.has}} hidden{{/results.has}}>{{results.label}}</span></span>
        </div>
        <span class="dim-poster__veil"></span>
        <div class="dim-poster__base">
            {{#hasmark}}
            <span class="dim-poster__mark{{#markfolder}} dim-poster__mark--folder{{/markfolder}}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {{/hasmark}}
            <h3 class="dim-poster__name">
                {{#hascontrolurl}}
                <a class="dim-poster__control" href="{{controlurl}}" data-region="dim-poster-control"{{#results.has}} aria-describedby="dim-area-results-{{id}}"{{/results.has}}><span class="dim-poster__nm">{{name}}</span><span class="visually-hidden" data-region="dim-poster-emptynote"{{#expandable}} hidden{{/expandable}}> {{#str}}category_card_nocourseslink, theme_dimensions{{/str}}</span></a>
                {{/hascontrolurl}}
                {{^hascontrolurl}}
                <span class="dim-poster__control" data-region="dim-poster-control"{{#results.has}} aria-describedby="dim-area-results-{{id}}"{{/results.has}}><span class="dim-poster__nm">{{name}}</span></span>
                {{/hascontrolurl}}
            </h3>
            {{#hasdescription}}
            <p class="dim-poster__desc">{{description}}</p>
            {{/hasdescription}}
            <span class="dim-poster__trig" aria-hidden="true"><span class="dim-poster__trigtext" data-region="dim-poster-trigger" data-open="{{#str}}category_card_open, theme_dimensions{{/str}}" data-close="{{#str}}category_card_close, theme_dimensions{{/str}}" data-empty="{{#str}}category_card_nocourses, theme_dimensions{{/str}}">{{^expandable}}{{#str}}category_card_nocourses, theme_dimensions{{/str}}{{/expandable}}{{#expandable}}{{#isopen}}{{#str}}category_card_close, theme_dimensions{{/str}}{{/isopen}}{{^isopen}}{{#str}}category_card_open, theme_dimensions{{/str}}{{/isopen}}{{/expandable}}</span><span class="dim-poster__chev"><i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true"></i></span></span>
        </div>
        {{#hasvideo}}
        <div class="dim-poster__filmctl dim-cover-js-only" data-region="dim-cover-controls">
            <button type="button" class="dim-poster__filmbtn" data-action="dim-cover-play" aria-pressed="false"><i class="fa-solid fa-play" data-region="dim-cover-glyph" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">{{#str}}category_cover_play, theme_dimensions, {{name}}{{/str}}</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="dim-poster__filmbtn" data-action="dim-cover-mute" aria-pressed="true"><i class="fa-solid fa-volume-xmark" data-region="dim-cover-glyph" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">{{#str}}category_cover_mute, theme_dimensions, {{name}}{{/str}}</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="dim-poster__filmbtn" data-action="dim-cover-fullscreen"><i class="fa-solid fa-expand" data-region="dim-cover-glyph" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden">{{#str}}category_cover_fullscreen, theme_dimensions, {{name}}{{/str}}</span></button>
        </div>
        <div class="dim-poster__bar dim-cover-js-only" data-region="dim-cover-progress" aria-hidden="true"><span class="dim-poster__barfill" data-region="dim-cover-bar"></span></div>
        {{/hasvideo}}
    </div>
</article>
